ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417835 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417835 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186417827 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417835 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "cc6bf158-bc5a-5b83-aecb-e172b7a9b66e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417836 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186417834 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417836 #edb/ref 1069 "q-124153" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417836 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417836 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=4u+v-1,\\,y=-u-3v+1.\n$$\n\nLet $P(-3,1)$ be a point in the $uv$-plane. Suppose that the image of $P$ under the action of $T$ is the point ${P}^{′}$ in the $xy$-plane. What are the coordinates of ${P}^{′}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417836 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6cb153c3-10ae-52e4-a409-49d1a1150376" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417836 #edb/ref 1074 "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nNotice that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4u+v-1 \\\\ -u-3v+1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4u+v \\\\ -u-3v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the image of $P$ under the action of $T,$ we first create a column vector $u$ containing the coordinates of $P:$ \n\n$$\nu=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nApplying $T$ to $u,$ we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-12 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of ${P}^{′}$ are $(-12,1).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417837 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186417835 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417837 #edb/ref 1069 "q-162181" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417837 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417837 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the affine transformation $T,$ defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nWhat is the area scale factor of the transformation?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417837 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "914af94d-7042-54e6-acb1-fed694c9a4de" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417837 #edb/ref 1074 "The matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nComputing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}|=1\\cdot 4-3\\cdot 2=-2.\n$$\n\nSo, the area scale factor of the transformation is\n\n$$\n|det(A)|=|-2|=2.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
